WEBVTT

00:00:01.433 --> 00:00:04.066
-[Narrator] Welcome to Module 3 Accessible Microsoft

00:00:04.066 --> 00:00:07.432
PowerPoint Documents. In this video, you will

00:00:07.433 --> 00:00:09.299
learn how to make your PowerPoint documents

00:00:09.300 --> 00:00:10.833
accessible to all learners.

00:00:13.133 --> 00:00:15.599
In this section, we will set your document title

00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:19.300
and language. Setting the document title in

00:00:19.300 --> 00:00:22.033
PowerPoint is much like we did in Word. In your

00:00:22.033 --> 00:00:26.399
PowerPoint presentation, Click File, then select

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:30.233
Info. From the right-hand panel, locate the

00:00:30.233 --> 00:00:33.766
Properties section. Click on the space indicated to

00:00:33.766 --> 00:00:38.466
the right of Title. Enter a descriptive title here,

00:00:38.600 --> 00:00:41.333
such as "Accessible Slide Design."

00:00:43.566 --> 00:00:46.832
To set the document language, go to the Review tab,

00:00:47.466 --> 00:00:51.532
select Language, and choose Set Proofing Language.

00:00:52.766 --> 00:00:55.432
From the list, select your desired language, such

00:00:55.433 --> 00:00:59.533
as English (United States). Check the box labeled

00:00:59.833 --> 00:01:03.466
"Do not check spelling or grammar," and then click

00:01:03.466 --> 00:01:07.166
OK to apply your settings. Now that we have

00:01:07.166 --> 00:01:09.266
given the title and set the preferred language for

00:01:09.266 --> 00:01:12.066
our PowerPoint, people can understand the document

00:01:12.066 --> 00:01:14.599
context without opening it and interpret the

00:01:14.600 --> 00:01:19.466
content accurately. In this section, we will set

00:01:19.466 --> 00:01:24.066
clear unique titles for each slide. Each slide

00:01:24.066 --> 00:01:25.832
requires a different title for accurate

00:01:25.833 --> 00:01:29.133
communication with assistive technologies. Slide

00:01:29.133 --> 00:01:31.033
titles can be checked by selecting View from the

00:01:31.033 --> 00:01:34.733
menu and clicking Outline View. A panel will

00:01:34.733 --> 00:01:36.799
appear to the left of the screen, indicating the

00:01:36.800 --> 00:01:39.500
names of each slide in the presentation, and they

00:01:39.500 --> 00:01:42.733
appear at the top of each slide. If there is a

00:01:42.733 --> 00:01:44.933
title duplication, it will need to be adjusted.

00:01:45.600 --> 00:01:48.533
For instance, if two slides are titled "Common

00:01:48.533 --> 00:01:53.399
Barriers," you could add "Part 1" and "Part 2,"

00:01:53.700 --> 00:01:55.033
like this example here.

00:01:58.633 --> 00:02:01.599
In this section, we will add alternative text and

00:02:01.600 --> 00:02:06.100
create accessible hyperlinks. Images, graphs, or

00:02:06.100 --> 00:02:08.733
charts should include alternative text or be

00:02:08.733 --> 00:02:12.299
described as decorative. To add alternative text,

00:02:12.533 --> 00:02:15.299
right-click on the image and select Alt Text in

00:02:15.300 --> 00:02:18.133
the pop-up menu. The Alt Text pane will show to

00:02:18.133 --> 00:02:20.766
the right of your screen. If the image contains

00:02:20.766 --> 00:02:23.666
meaningful information, add alternative text in

00:02:23.666 --> 00:02:26.499
the empty box describing the content and purpose.

00:02:27.333 --> 00:02:30.333
In this example, the alternative text would be

00:02:30.866 --> 00:02:33.766
"Students with disabilities drop out at about twice

00:02:33.766 --> 00:02:38.066
the rate of their non-disabled peers." It is a best

00:02:38.066 --> 00:02:41.699
practice to keep descriptive phrases brief. Do not

00:02:41.700 --> 00:02:45.600
begin the description with words "Image of ..." or

00:02:46.033 --> 00:02:49.633
"Picture of ..."; screen readers automatically use the

00:02:49.633 --> 00:02:53.999
term "Image." If the image is simply decorative, leave

00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:57.600
the description field box blank and check Mark as

00:02:57.600 --> 00:03:00.933
decorative; close the Alt Text pane to apply

00:03:00.933 --> 00:03:01.433
changes.

00:03:03.466 --> 00:03:05.766
Microsoft PowerPoint automatically creates a

00:03:05.766 --> 00:03:08.966
hyperlink when a URL is added to a slide. However,

00:03:09.233 --> 00:03:12.266
to meet accessibility requirements, hyperlinks

00:03:12.266 --> 00:03:15.232
must be clear and actionable, allowing users to

00:03:15.233 --> 00:03:18.466
understand where the link is leading them. To add

00:03:18.466 --> 00:03:20.499
meaningful language, right-click on the link.

00:03:21.033 --> 00:03:23.899
Select Edit. At the top of this window, you will

00:03:23.900 --> 00:03:26.833
enter a descriptive title such as "Visit the

00:03:26.833 --> 00:03:31.733
Official WCAG 2.1 guidelines from W3C"

00:03:31.833 --> 00:03:36.333
instead of "Click Here." "Visit the Official

00:03:36.433 --> 00:03:41.633
WCAG 2.1 guidelines from W3C" alerts someone

00:03:41.633 --> 00:03:43.966
listening to a screen reader that there is an

00:03:43.966 --> 00:03:48.366
actionable item in the document. Designing a

00:03:48.366 --> 00:03:50.632
visually appealing presentation can often go

00:03:50.633 --> 00:03:54.333
against accessibility requirements. Color choice

00:03:54.333 --> 00:03:56.666
combinations can create difficulty for users to

00:03:56.666 --> 00:04:00.599
read text on the screen. Background and font color

00:04:00.600 --> 00:04:03.733
should have clear contrast between them. Using a

00:04:03.733 --> 00:04:08.366
black background with a white font works well. For

00:04:08.366 --> 00:04:11.766
example, this due date is in a light red font on a

00:04:11.766 --> 00:04:15.532
yellow background. These colors do not provide a

00:04:15.533 --> 00:04:19.799
good contrast, making it difficult to read. A

00:04:19.800 --> 00:04:22.300
suggestion would be to make the font color black

00:04:22.300 --> 00:04:24.733
and bold and remove the background.

00:04:28.566 --> 00:04:31.032
In this section, we will adjust font size and

00:04:31.033 --> 00:04:32.866
fix reading order for accessibility.

00:04:36.533 --> 00:04:39.899
Let's change some fonts. From the Slides pane on the

00:04:39.900 --> 00:04:42.433
left side of the screen, right-click on the slide,

00:04:42.433 --> 00:04:46.299
and select Duplicate Slide. On the new slide, delete

00:04:46.300 --> 00:04:51.366
the top three items from the list; select all text,

00:04:51.366 --> 00:04:55.832
and set font size to 24. Now, go to the previous

00:04:55.833 --> 00:05:00.833
slide, and delete the bottom three items. Now,

00:05:01.166 --> 00:05:03.466
select the remaining text from the list and set

00:05:03.466 --> 00:05:08.666
font size to 24. Also, make sure each slide has a

00:05:08.666 --> 00:05:12.632
unique title. This will ensure that your text is

00:05:12.633 --> 00:05:13.299
accessible.

00:05:17.100 --> 00:05:20.266
After setting up clear, readable text, the next

00:05:20.266 --> 00:05:22.566
step is to verify the slides reading order.

00:05:22.966 --> 00:05:25.666
Verifying the read order of a slide is important,

00:05:25.666 --> 00:05:28.466
especially if additional content placeholders are

00:05:28.466 --> 00:05:31.732
added to the slide. To check or change a slide's

00:05:31.733 --> 00:05:34.533
reading order, in the Home tab at the top of your

00:05:34.533 --> 00:05:38.466
screen, click Arrange and click Selection Pane.

00:05:38.966 --> 00:05:41.299
Your Selection pane will show to the right of your

00:05:41.300 --> 00:05:44.300
screen, listing all content found on your slide.

00:05:45.033 --> 00:05:47.566
The screen reader will read content from bottom to

00:05:47.566 --> 00:05:51.332
top. In this example, right now the screen reader

00:05:51.333 --> 00:05:56.133
reads Picture 3, then Title 5, and finally

00:05:56.433 --> 00:05:59.833
Rectangle 3. To fix this in the Selection

00:05:59.833 --> 00:06:03.233
pane, first drag Title 5 down to the bottom;

00:06:04.000 --> 00:06:07.366
next, place Rectangle 3 just above Title 5;

00:06:07.966 --> 00:06:11.932
and keep Picture 3 above both objects. This

00:06:11.933 --> 00:06:13.499
sets the correct reading order.

00:06:17.433 --> 00:06:19.766
In this section, we will run the accessibility

00:06:19.766 --> 00:06:22.366
checker and fix remaining issues manually.

00:06:24.733 --> 00:06:27.199
As with all documents, accessibility should be

00:06:27.200 --> 00:06:30.600
checked. At the top of the screen, open the Review

00:06:30.600 --> 00:06:35.900
tab, then choose Check Accessibility. Any errors,

00:06:35.900 --> 00:06:38.700
warnings, and tips will show in the checker on the

00:06:38.700 --> 00:06:42.533
right side of your screen. In this example, I

00:06:42.533 --> 00:06:45.933
still have one accessibility issue, "Missing

00:06:45.933 --> 00:06:50.533
Slide Title". To fix it, select the error and then

00:06:50.933 --> 00:06:54.899
choose Set as Slide Title; click Approve and the

00:06:54.900 --> 00:06:58.366
issue will be resolved. While the PowerPoint

00:06:58.366 --> 00:07:01.032
accessibility checker is helpful, it does not

00:07:01.033 --> 00:07:05.566
evaluate everything. For example, it cannot verify

00:07:05.566 --> 00:07:09.032
the font style or the size of text elements. On

00:07:09.033 --> 00:07:12.333
Slide 6, some list items are set to 11 point

00:07:12.333 --> 00:07:15.933
font, but the checker does not flag that. To fix

00:07:15.933 --> 00:07:20.999
this, I will change them to 24 point. Therefore,

00:07:21.000 --> 00:07:23.700
it is important for content creators to manually

00:07:23.700 --> 00:07:26.833
verify appropriate font styles and sizes are used,

00:07:27.166 --> 00:07:29.899
and that color contrast meets accessibility

00:07:29.900 --> 00:07:30.466
standards.
